contentText:
Artists meet each other all the time backstage after shows, but one Kendrick Lamar dressing-room encounter has stuck with Marcus Mumford.

The Mumford & Sons singer joined the SmartLess podcast on Monday (July 27), which found him detailing his first encounter with K. Dot after the rapper&rsquo;s performance at Bonnaroo Music Festival.&nbsp;

Mumford explained how there was a specific request from Lamar to meet the singer. &ldquo;When I was invited, very explicitly invited, backstage was after Kendrick Lamar played Bonnaroo,&rdquo; he said. &ldquo;There was a message that came down from on high that Kendrick would like to see you. When Kendrick calls, you come, right, because he&rsquo;s the king.&rdquo;

Mumford recalled being caught off guard when he entered Lamar&rsquo;s dressing room, as the rapper sparked conversation as he was in the middle of changing clothes.

&ldquo;He took almost all of his clothes as I walked in. It was amazing,&rdquo; Mumford said. &ldquo;I thought, like, the gumption to be like, &lsquo;Yeah, come on back after the show and it will be the very moment I take all my clothes off and I&rsquo;m just down to my undies and we&rsquo;ll have a chat.&rsquo;&rdquo;

The 39-year-old credited Lamar for being himself even though it was their first time interacting. &ldquo;Real confidence. Swag,&rdquo; Mumford complimented the West Coast rap legend.

Lamar has performed at Bonnaroo on three separate occasions, 2012, 2015 and 2023, with Mumford & Sons sharing the bill in 2015.

Mumford is currently on the North American leg of Mumford & Sons&rsquo; Prizefighter Tour, which boasts upcoming shows in Minnesota, Iowa and Atlanta, as well as three dates at Madison Square Garden in NYC.

